{
  "dom_id": "step-e11111",
  "name": "Example: Applications of Confidence Intervals",
  "problem": "The diameters of balls for bearings produced by machines ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/46833dd7644e5c60bb4525fe4e7649a99752b26096331755a4b44c2abe183f11.svg) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/ab4817775494786b06f0b9cecf225ea5979c035b69c36c1fa078f835524be9e9.svg) have standard deviations of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/d119f2a860c3a45855fddc0be7b90afe3ef3b9c9a1d9e12f6f292887360e797d.svg) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/47d7f608a187818bc771a90371ec6ed6fd92a8446815fb911253e4f545627c81.svg) respectively. Engineers want to know whether the population mean ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/61959f998d5bf057f78b23b849c800b479b5640bee3f604626eb721872cffc20.svg) for the diameter of balls produced by machine ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/46833dd7644e5c60bb4525fe4e7649a99752b26096331755a4b44c2abe183f11.svg) is larger than the population mean ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/550e73c341b931075845607f5f4bcece014f3088cfb1148197b696933d13545a.svg) for the diameter of balls produced by machine ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/029615e92d8b6d5c444a4daf74a9a8d63048e8d4be5f97c8207fe7af2e189e18.svg) They construct a ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/4aa35f22590ee68ad0ff0b07b01c41e9caf9e2ad6c73a305f297e918d684e045.svg) confidence interval for the difference between the population means.   \n\nGiven that the engineers sampled ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/8c0d9d65f3495da5c81dd0e397e9c32f09f2440810847b109055a8cdf9b63c1d.svg) balls produced by machine ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/46833dd7644e5c60bb4525fe4e7649a99752b26096331755a4b44c2abe183f11.svg) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/4554df746f5a593617a7882989a71995d6e7a6be8ef47225843dafb9e8d746e3.svg) balls made by machine ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/ab4817775494786b06f0b9cecf225ea5979c035b69c36c1fa078f835524be9e9.svg) and found that their mean diameters are ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/3ac1972c8c6e03b02a5569c5ccf4f0cd79744fc783050367109d053c72c56e2e.svg) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/b3294c6196c0bb447f4261b566f3f910eff97c9591565bc2b35ac7798c3a5e97.svg) respectively, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The end-points of the ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/4aa35f22590ee68ad0ff0b07b01c41e9caf9e2ad6c73a305f297e918d684e045.svg) confidence interval for the difference between the population means are approximately ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/be02ea5f949b002400b734a0b683d09930c91c625e8be7d7a44a4eae822476c9.svg)\n\nII. All values contained within the ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/4aa35f22590ee68ad0ff0b07b01c41e9caf9e2ad6c73a305f297e918d684e045.svg) confidence interval are positive.\n\nIII. The confidence interval data suggests that ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/00d6a9d8ff1bdcb7095099ba2d0b2192b4df6bf4328ee093825ec36db7191df5.svg)\n\n*Hint: Given a random variable ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/bf4994a6e13924c5bc1f82242e6b12a6e452ebdb5c9f607b35c2614dab4ba30e.svg) the table below shows the ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/9032cb23a878659e74b670d3779a8cd4793b28af921eab1a6b3f2041a815e03b.svg)-scores ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/f948084d308bf70eed90f1ddc186f4d4b6ffd5b03b4a84db77741ca7acb0697c.svg) such that ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/2e84a088a2421fdf8a026b804a2a39d41831915f78d6ca5abcf7c95644ea3f98.svg) for some particular values of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/1d3e45623fb292952d8c207690797505cc7c484a6410f4a95aff94a51b4a0ee5.svg)*\n\n| ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/48c7b594e8628a17b991d4e65e7bee6ffe6680dd410f036cfae83154bbd55fc6.svg) | ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/14eb5f107102d64032e5c62207a5f22c7080993cccdec49809d85677e32228dc.svg) | ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/f40b54dcb945a64594b78fd581e4f950c4d9c07d15f30d9f1dc019f46c02cdde.svg) | ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/1156c0c032864aee44a0c788d626a41dc2f342323fa089a19d82027b0ae5a2e4.svg) | ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/96bea0a68c23edf8d74b7757824baa031b2b7d0bbabd8a9babe5b9bf72a0a13e.svg) | ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/bf7be53403f336e34ad868c68d24905fb2eafba87ae7c65ebfa0796fd137efe0.svg) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/f948084d308bf70eed90f1ddc186f4d4b6ffd5b03b4a84db77741ca7acb0697c.svg) | ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/12781236356b8a089115083f90b012544e848846f64395d4b9e0a5f2ca689c93.svg) | ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/b5f9496f7a1bda32cf8f921e43a5bb42c820b118ebe241131cd7a38b869061b7.svg) | ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/0e11b9a3e1e1a424a8db948ce46afebd8abc9faa855574ea12b8760c1da2ebf9.svg) | ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/185c18f81476cc288ddc92a0105a258c4b0e89893c75c7df3a6b366d6cdcf9ee.svg) | ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/1345290aa983a990a0e9592b1156be4bd26490599086e86ec7ccf83313f1412e.svg) |",
  "worked_solution": "Notice that\n\n- the samples are independent,\n\n- both sample sizes are \"sufficiently large,\" i.e., ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/7e953b8222eba132ef65fbeead25790198f988c2e0cd5625aa5de0fda0fefa1a.svg) and\n\n- both population variances are known.\n\nAs a result, given a value ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/7995b2daef1650484d2fa6518cb775356ae12ecdf597eba9e2e04f4f35dee93c.svg) between ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/156b31ede73de5301befe67f02745a0202f1806a62f9fdecc6fc9ee3f21117ba.svg) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/76543f4805f22715457d55feb2a3c87d0d873bdcb9c1eed7a4f68539269dcf59.svg) the corresponding ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/1fb6279301c8fe6dce4a6f502a17e6e4abeaa62a44a9ab5023a1d3ccf4aac5c4.svg) confidence interval for the difference ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/9d6dac96cd69f7064940eae6e63d88c95f1fc4a92b102ba3693dd819ac128126.svg) between the corresponding population means can be written as\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/5d808254159d48a94531e110e5d9c4c8fabc2f800c5615802abccfa7bc8ea622.svg)\n\nwhere \n\n- ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/4b7b988b2e9ef88f674ce655d7d2f15af2f4e9172bd7a9d6cce2fe0aa72e82df.svg) is the margin of error,\n\n- ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/6937033abbb07640e7bfa8def543b2a045bb5e1775a939ab76a5fcca1cb0a0ea.svg) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/fca756bcf0457e144eb84a5bfd67bb3f4432d22de2e7d0f3c5fb2e9c78727da9.svg) are the sample means, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/6d3486d14fef4cbd7f15af9097617bd5e675baa1f13cb86f69f09bef24ee4829.svg) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/a21f07d3948532bb6aa91995da9b6d602ad4b8628d9ea967ad3f3d135f9ba533.svg) are the population means, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/20f6be5e75cac9315a72adf7baab3c361dbb69fe57709526e03c9a023af587af.svg) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/65622d587fccd0fe592e6a5dce2ed965999dd2e90a288087469f8c4c70eb3503.svg) are the population variances,  ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/de44911177478b672559d6311b30df7c906693cd480fe64d8dcf78c08412d61e.svg) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/072df845480f1dd134dc71854a3d9aeacde7563aaca739d5c718f5068d5ee300.svg) are the sample sizes,\n\n- ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/af38b9349332c35a9833820ab5fa0f3540b7655405c8b2ca17587f3db84f53bf.svg) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/c1a5b6740351318fb48420ebbed2f09086cd253fb88b802c8f6bf138640d75fa.svg)\n\nNow, to construct the confidence interval, we proceed as follows:\n\n- **Step 1.** Find the point estimate:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/c1d47fdc3028b6d69a77ad99d91ad6031d852da3aad276e0ff8e792b12edecc3.svg)\n\n- **Step 2.** Find the margin of error. Since we are interested in finding a ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/4aa35f22590ee68ad0ff0b07b01c41e9caf9e2ad6c73a305f297e918d684e045.svg) confidence interval, we have \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/bb227d4b2458830d95e344377c1633020fb3ce3bc3f27acfb7ec28f3473c6548.svg)\nWe also need to find the ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/9032cb23a878659e74b670d3779a8cd4793b28af921eab1a6b3f2041a815e03b.svg)-score value ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/ff6062321d513483e6075fddac7ccaa5d848044aa39968f15e2e120e23e09cc4.svg) such that ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/98124d1c0a053f7a1651a849ef0f233f42ca9c8bae4154aaed3bd995b88dcdb7.svg) where ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/c1a5b6740351318fb48420ebbed2f09086cd253fb88b802c8f6bf138640d75fa.svg)\n\nFrom the percentage points table of the normal distribution, we obtain that ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/5b048df55a97617e12801c6e121edf26dfc90b10795b7fb3c3e57990511bc3ca.svg) \n\n| ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/48c7b594e8628a17b991d4e65e7bee6ffe6680dd410f036cfae83154bbd55fc6.svg) | ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/14eb5f107102d64032e5c62207a5f22c7080993cccdec49809d85677e32228dc.svg) | ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/f40b54dcb945a64594b78fd581e4f950c4d9c07d15f30d9f1dc019f46c02cdde.svg) | ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/1156c0c032864aee44a0c788d626a41dc2f342323fa089a19d82027b0ae5a2e4.svg) | ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/96bea0a68c23edf8d74b7757824baa031b2b7d0bbabd8a9babe5b9bf72a0a13e.svg) | ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/c9b3bdfe48f79c3efdc3f67699556323b7f2df004dc4e9957e2e2fd18a98494c.svg) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/f948084d308bf70eed90f1ddc186f4d4b6ffd5b03b4a84db77741ca7acb0697c.svg) | ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/12781236356b8a089115083f90b012544e848846f64395d4b9e0a5f2ca689c93.svg) | ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/b5f9496f7a1bda32cf8f921e43a5bb42c820b118ebe241131cd7a38b869061b7.svg) | ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/0e11b9a3e1e1a424a8db948ce46afebd8abc9faa855574ea12b8760c1da2ebf9.svg) | ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/185c18f81476cc288ddc92a0105a258c4b0e89893c75c7df3a6b366d6cdcf9ee.svg) | ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/15b83a8ca53afabe815ab94d820effad249c1e7b05bb06c20bf94badc051a9da.svg) |\n\nNow, we can compute the margin of error:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/4a3f5d764d317efe5be018c3be111afdb40da1316dc74fe9ccf8037274260ee7.svg) \n\n- **Step 3.** Construct the confidence interval:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/0c73cf36767ddad8a08ec9fe256a146af7d251921180cdb7397c69a5a2fa6baf.svg)\n\nLet's now examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. The end-points of our confidence interval are ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/be02ea5f949b002400b734a0b683d09930c91c625e8be7d7a44a4eae822476c9.svg)\n\n- Statement II is false. The confidence interval contains zero.\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/a08641be702b83463c7c420e7ae8f77d69564f4c1734f3d809efe7a4027fed7e.svg)\n\n- Statement III is false. Since the confidence interval contains zero, it remains possible that ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14187244/assets/52ee5d6a0009f029e4a9917fbff9deecf964de59a9bea34c3461695582c597ba.svg)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
